SUMMARY OF TERMS (the legal code above governs; this summary does not)

  You are free to SHARE -- copy and redistribute the material in any medium or
  format -- provided you follow the terms below.

  ATTRIBUTION. You must give appropriate credit, provide a link to the licence,
  and indicate if changes were made. Cite the Zenodo record with its DOI and
  version, and the accompanying manuscript. The provenance fields in this
  dataset must travel with the values.

  NONCOMMERCIAL. You may not use the material for commercial purposes.

  NODERIVATIVES. If you remix, transform or build upon the material, you may
  not distribute the modified material.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT RESTRICT

  Verification. Downloading this dataset, re-running the published checks,
  re-deriving the denominators and reporting a disagreement are reading, not
  adapting. Nothing in this licence impedes checking the work.

  Quoting under fair dealing or fair use, citing, and peer review.

WHAT REQUIRES PERMISSION

  Publishing a modified or derived table; pooling this dataset into an
  aggregated public resource that redistributes a harmonised copy; and any
  commercial use. Contact the author.

SEPARATE TERMS APPLY TO

  Analysis code, which is licensed Apache-2.0 and published at
  https://github.com/piranfar/portabilityrisk. Running Apache-2.0 code over
  this data does not place the output under Apache-2.0.

  Source genome data. NCBI Assembly, BioSample and BioProject records remain
  governed by NCBI's terms. This dataset contains accessions and computed
  values derived from them, not redistributed sequence. No licence is applied
  to third-party data or software by this deposit.

  Third-party software and reference databases named in
